+Source and verification for this grammar and its worked witnesses: [Original grammar and witnesses](https://github.com/MettaMazza/ernos-labs-sft-platform/blob/76f1b34e9e9682989adcbb088797b4ae4ce4fcf1/sft/information_science/conservation_loss_transformation/law.py#L98), [ConservationGrammar.candidatesComplete](https://github.com/MettaMazza/SFT-v4-LEAN-VERIFIED/blob/21cdf559922fb057f8560f42d056ffa035329eb3/SFT/InformationScience/ConservationGrammar.lean#L140), [ConservationWitnesses.allWitnessesPass](https://github.com/MettaMazza/SFT-v4-LEAN-VERIFIED/blob/21cdf559922fb057f8560f42d056ffa035329eb3/SFT/InformationScience/ConservationWitnesses.lean#L37).
+
+The original conservation grammar alternatives and their elimination arguments are:
+
+1. support: partial-input-support versus complete-canonical-source. Omission hides distinctions that may be lost. Every registered source form occurs once.
+2. map: partial-or-multivalued-rule versus total-single-valued-map. An incomplete or multivalued rule cannot account for every source. Each source has exactly one held image.
+3. provenance: image-only-output versus exact-predecessor-fibres. Image-only output erases which sources entered each result. Every image retains its complete source class.
+4. accounting: output-cardinality-only versus complete-source-pair-partition. A count erases which distinctions survive. Every source pair is classified exactly as retained or closed.
+5. loss: lower-score-assertion versus non-singleton-image-fibre. A score does not identify unavailable predecessors. Loss is the exact source distinctions closed inside an image fibre.
+6. reversal: assumed-inverse versus singleton-fibre-or-held-record. An inverse cannot choose among merged predecessors. Singleton fibres reverse directly; merged fibres require retained predecessor labels.
+7. composition: fresh-downstream-distinction versus retained-pair-subset. A deterministic image map has no source for a distinction already closed. A downstream map can preserve or close an upstream distinction but cannot reopen it.
+8. conservation: unchanged-scalar versus retained-plus-closed-exhaustion. An unchanged scalar can hide exchanges among distinctions. The two exact ledgers disjointly exhaust all source distinctions.
+9. generality: sampled-transformations versus source-successor-map-cell. Examples do not prove a fresh source image accounted. A fresh source adds one held map cell and all new pair comparisons.
+10. addition: unrecorded-created-distinction versus no-extra-information-source. A new distinction without source or record violates provenance. All output distinctions trace to separated source images or declared external input.
+
+The five operational witnesses are calculated in section117: all six source pairs retained by identity, exactly two pairs closed by prefix projection, four versus two distinct images giving the reversibility boundary, both complete two-member reverse records, and complete downstream erasure after the two prefix images merge. ConservationWitnesses.allWitnessesPass checks these calculations. The arbitrary-support arguments are the exhaustive pair split, exact composition, singleton-fibre equivalence and successor equations in sections113–117.
 
